Project: KylGis POS 1.0
Topic: Installer README
Maintainer: KylGis POS Project
Date: 8 October 2026

KylGis POS is a Java point-of-sale system distributed under GNU GPL v3.
It can run as a standalone POS or as part of a multinode deployment where
configuration, hardware services and optional capabilities are assigned by role.

Requirements
------------
- Java 21 LTS or newer, compatible with the operating system and CPU architecture.
- A supported MariaDB/MySQL/PostgreSQL database reachable by the configured node.
- JavaFX is not required by the POS core. It is required only by the optional
  Kitchen capability.

Portable hardware model
-----------------------
KylGis can use printers, scales, scanners and customer displays locally when
the required driver/native library exists for the platform. Nodes without a
compatible native driver (for example ARM nodes using legacy RXTX peripherals)
can delegate those devices to KylGis hardware-service nodes.

Database upgrades
-----------------
Historical KylGis schemas may contain InnoDB tables using ROW_FORMAT=COMPACT.
Before upgrading a MariaDB server, run MariaDbRowFormatTool in check mode against
an explicit KylGis configuration. Applying ROW_FORMAT=DYNAMIC is intentionally
blocked unless both --apply and --backup-confirmed are supplied during an
authorized maintenance window.

Configuration
-------------
A traditional standalone installation can use its local properties file.
Provisioned deployments use a minimal node bootstrap and obtain their effective
configuration from the KylGis MASTER. Remote-provisioned nodes maintain an
encrypted last-known-good cache for temporary MASTER/network outages.

Start KylGis with the launcher supplied for your operating system. The launcher
uses the canonical role-aware runtime contained in kylgispos.jar.

Licensing and attribution
-------------------------
KylGis POS contains work derived from Openbravo POS, uniCenta oPOS and Chromis
projects, plus subsequent KylGis modifications. Historical authorship and
license information is retained in the licensing and contribution files shipped
with the application.

Project information: https://pos.kylgis.com
